+## At the entrance display
+
+Your door check-in wakes WelcomePi and shows your first name and today's agenda. You can also tap your fob on the reader beside the display. The door reader records your arrival. A local tap controls the display. The kiosk logs the member name and reader location for recognized scans.
+
+**Your reservations** covers the next 12 hours, including time already underway. Pending and unpaid reservations carry a label. **Volunteer opportunities** shows work you can claim. Tasks restricted to today's weekday get the first two places when available. Space permitting, the screen also shows today's Eventbrite classes and a QR code for the portal Home page.
+
+**A second tap shows personal information to everyone near the screen.** On your own agenda, lift and tap your fob again if you want to share that view. Ledger participants see their character sheet and current avatar or rank icon. Other members see the text of kudos they have received, including private messages, followed by their current tool checkouts. Tap once more to clear your details.
+
+A different local fob starts its owner's welcome immediately. On the details screen you have 30 seconds before a waiting door arrival takes over. After two minutes without a qualifying scan, the display returns to today's five recent arrivals, lifetime volunteer point leaders, available work, and the portal QR code. After four hours it sleeps until the next qualifying scan.
+
 ## For admins

 Admins can open the tab on a member's profile. For admins it also lists **Additional Details** for each scan, such as the **Card Holder**, plus the validity and location. Use it to help a member whose fob does not work: find their recent scans and read the validity of the refused ones. Open it only for a real need, such as a member asking for help, and do not share what you see with others.
